fuse: leave a DAX file's entries to its layouts' own breaking

Since 6.15 a DAX page is counted by its mappings (fs/dax: properly refcount
fs dax pages). FUSE drops a regular file's cached pages at each open
without FOPEN_KEEP_CACHE (fuse_open(), fuse_create_open()), and as its
attributes show its size changed (fuse_change_attributes_i()); for a DAX
file those are its DAX entries. invalidate_inode_pages2() lets each entry
go (__dax_invalidate_entry()) before it unmaps the page tables that map it,
after its loop, and truncate_pagecache() finds entries no one broke the
layouts of. A 2 MiB entry still mapped is split into small pages that
still hold counts, and later faults there find pages whose file and counts
are wrong. A virtiofs guest whose processes map files through its DAX
window gets, as one process opens a file another maps:

  WARNING: CPU: 6 PID: 1212 at fs/dax.c:415 dax_folio_put.isra.0+0x118/0x130
  Call Trace: dax_invalidate_mapping_entry_sync <- invalidate_inode_pages2_range
    <- invalidate_inode_pages2 <- fuse_open <- do_dentry_open <- vfs_open
  WARNING: CPU: 1 PID: 1627 at fs/dax.c:437 dax_insert_entry+0x32d/0x370
  Call Trace: dax_fault_iter <- dax_iomap_pmd_fault <- __fuse_dax_fault
  WARNING: CPU: 4 PID: 1758 at fs/dax.c:460 dax_insert_entry+0x362/0x370
  Call Trace: dax_fault_iter <- dax_iomap_pte_fault <- __fuse_dax_fault

and the processes that fault there get SIGBUS: 5 of 5 cargo builds of
rust-analyzer on a shards volume with a window.

A DAX file has no page cache to go stale: its bytes are the host's,
through the window. So drop nothing of a DAX file as it is opened, nor as
its attributes show its size changed. Its entries go as its layouts are
broken: by FUSE's own truncation (fuse_do_setattr(), an OPEN's O_TRUNC),
its fallocate, the reclaim of a range and its eviction. A page mapped past
a size another client cut reads what the host gives there until then; a
new fault past i_size still gets SIGBUS. Mainline has the same code at
v7.2-rc4.

